Registers and Macros

	•	"xy: Yank (copy) into register x.
	•	"xp: Paste the content of register x.
	•	q<letter>: Start recording a macro into register <letter>.
	•	q: Stop recording a macro.
	•	@<letter>: Play back the macro stored in register <letter>.
	•	@@: Repeat the last macro.

File Management

	•	:w: Save the file.
	•	:q: Quit Vim.
	•	:wq: Save and quit Vim.
	•	:q!: Quit without saving.
	•	:e filename: Open a file named filename.
	•	:bn: Switch to the next buffer.
	•	:bp: Switch to the previous buffer.
	•	:bd: Close the current buffer.

Split Windows

	•	:split: Split the window horizontally.
	•	:vsplit: Split the window vertically.
	•	Ctrl+w h: Move to the split window to the left.
	•	Ctrl+w l: Move to the split window to the right.
	•	Ctrl+w j: Move to the split window below.
	•	Ctrl+w k: Move to the split window above.
	•	Ctrl+w q: Close the current split window.

Tabs

	•	:tabnew: Open a new tab.
	•	:tabclose: Close the current tab.
	•	:tabn: Move to the next tab.
	•	:tabp: Move to the previous tab.

Additional Navigation Commands

	•	w: Move the cursor to the beginning of the next word.
	•	b: Move the cursor to the beginning of the previous word.
	•	e: Move the cursor to the end of the current word.
	•	%: Jump to the matching parenthesis, bracket, or brace.
	•	*: Search forward for the word under the cursor.
	•	#: Search backward for the word under the cursor.

Advanced Editing Commands

	•	ciw: Change the inner word (delete the word under the cursor and enter Insert Mode).
	•	diw: Delete the inner word (delete the word under the cursor).
	•	y$: Yank (copy) from the cursor position to the end of the line.
	•	p: Paste the yanked or deleted text after the cursor.
	•	P: Paste the yanked or deleted text before the cursor.

Visual Mode Enhancements

	•	gv: Re-select the last visual selection.
	•	o: In Visual Mode, move to the other end of the highlighted text.

Marks and Jumps

	•	m{a-z}: Set a mark at the current cursor position.
	•	'{a-z}: Jump to the beginning of the line where the mark is set.
	•	``{a-z}`: Jump to the exact position where the mark is set.

Buffers and Windows

	•	:ls: List all open buffers.
	•	:b{n}: Switch to buffer number {n}.
	•	Ctrl+^: Switch to the previously edited buffer.
	•	Ctrl+w s: Split the window horizontally.
	•	Ctrl+w v: Split the window vertically.
	•	Ctrl+w c: Close the current window.

Command-Line Mode Enhancements

	•	q:: Open the command-line window to view and edit previous commands.
	•	q/: Open the command-line window to view and edit previous search patterns.

Registers and Macros

	•	"ayy: Yank the current line into register a.
	•	"ap: Paste the contents of register a.
	•	q{a-z}: Start recording a macro into register {a-z}.
	•	q: Stop recording the macro.
	•	@{a-z}: Execute the macro stored in register {a-z}.

Miscellaneous

	•	Ctrl+g: Display the current file name and cursor position.
	•	ga: Display the ASCII value of the character under the cursor.
	•	zz: Center the current line in the window.
